From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linker: dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT) falls back to the host libraries

On Android dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, "calloc") finds libc's symbol. Here libc is glibc (behind libc_bio), which is not in the bionic
linker's solist, so RTLD_DEFAULT found only symbols with a bionic_ wrapper or in bionic-loaded libraries. Dart's FFI resolves
native functions without an asset by that process lookup (package:ffi's calloc): FluffyChat could not open its database, never
reached runApp and showed a black window. The same fallback patch 0017 gives RTLD_NEXT.

apklayer patch 0031 of patches/bionic_translation.
---
 linker/dlfcn.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/linker/dlfcn.c b/linker/dlfcn.c
--- a/linker/dlfcn.c
+++ b/linker/dlfcn.c
@@ -173,6 +173,13 @@

 	if (handle == RTLD_DEFAULT) {
 		sym = apkenv_lookup(symbol, &found, NULL);
+		if (!sym) { /* apklayer patch: the host libraries too, as Android's RTLD_DEFAULT finds libc's symbols (glibc's here) */
+			void *host = dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, symbol);
+			if (host) {
+				pthread_mutex_unlock(&apkenv_dl_lock);
+				return wrapper_create(symbol, host);
+			}
+		}
 	} else if (handle == RTLD_NEXT) {
 		void *ret_addr = __builtin_return_address(0);
 		soinfo *si = apkenv_find_containing_library(ret_addr);
